@startuml ray_vs_modal_detailed
title Ray vs Modal - Detailed Architecture Comparison

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

' ==================== RAY ARCHITECTURE ====================
package "Ray - Distributed Computing Framework" as ray #LightBlue {

    package "Communication Model" as rayComm #SkyBlue {
        component "Shared Memory\nObject Store" as rayObjStore
        component "Zero-Copy\nData Sharing" as rayZeroCopy
        component "gRPC/TCP\nCross-Node" as rayGrpc

        rayObjStore --> rayZeroCopy : same node
        rayObjStore --> rayGrpc : different nodes
    }

    package "Worker Isolation" as rayIsolation #LightCyan {
        component "Process-Level\nIsolation" as rayProcess
        component "Actors Can\nCommunicate" as rayActorComm
        component "Shared State\nvia Object Store" as raySharedState

        rayProcess --> rayActorComm
        rayActorComm --> raySharedState
    }

    package "GPU Autoscaling" as rayGpu #PaleGreen {
        component "Autoscaler V2" as rayAutoscaler
        component "request_resources()" as rayRequest
        component "Gang Scheduling\n(Kueue)" as rayGang
        component "GKE DRA\n(GB200 NVL72)" as rayGke

        rayAutoscaler --> rayRequest
        rayRequest --> rayGang
        rayGang --> rayGke
    }

    note right of rayComm
      **Ray IPC Advantages**
      ✓ Zero-copy for numpy arrays
      ✓ Shared memory (no serialization)
      ✓ Object refs passed between actors
      ✓ Automatic data locality
      ✓ Cross-node transparent
    end note
}

' ==================== MODAL ARCHITECTURE ====================
package "Modal - Serverless Sandbox Platform" as modal #LightGreen {

    package "Communication Model" as modalComm #PaleGreen {
        component "Modal Volumes\n(Distributed FS)" as modalVolumes
        component "modal.Dict\nmodal.Queue" as modalDict
        component "i6pn IPv6\n(Experimental)" as modalI6pn

        modalVolumes --> modalDict : data sharing
        modalDict --> modalI6pn : cluster mode
    }

    package "Container Isolation" as modalIsolation #LightYellow {
        component "gVisor\nKernel Isolation" as modalGvisor
        component "Containers\nCannot Communicate\n(by default)" as modalNoComm
        component "Blast Radius\nLimited to Container" as modalBlast

        modalGvisor --> modalNoComm
        modalNoComm --> modalBlast
    }

    package "GPU Scaling" as modalGpu #LightPink {
        component "Serverless\nAuto-scale" as modalServerless
        component "Per-Execution\nBilling" as modalBilling
        component "No Gang\nScheduling" as modalNoGang

        modalServerless --> modalBilling
        modalBilling --> modalNoGang
    }

    note right of modalIsolation
      **Modal Isolation (Strict)**
      ✓ gVisor syscall filtering
      ✓ No access to workspace
      ✓ Network egress control
      ✗ No shared memory
      ✗ No direct container-to-container
    end note
}

' ==================== COMPARISON TABLE ====================
package "Feature Comparison" as comparison #Wheat {
    note as compTable
      | Feature | Ray | Modal |
      |---------|-----|-------|
      | **IPC Mechanism** | Shared Memory Object Store | Distributed FS (Volumes) |
      | **Zero-Copy** | Yes (numpy arrays) | No |
      | **Container Communication** | Yes (native) | No (isolated by design) |
      | **Cluster Mode** | Native | Experimental (i6pn) |
      | **Isolation Level** | Process | gVisor (kernel) |
      | **State Sharing** | Object refs | Dict/Queue/Volumes |
      | **GPU Gang Scheduling** | Yes (Kueue) | No |
      | **Multi-Node Training** | Native support | Limited |
      | **Use Case** | Distributed ML Training | Untrusted Code Execution |
    end note
}

' ==================== KEY INSIGHT ====================
note bottom of comparison
  **Key Architectural Difference**

  **Ray**: Designed for **trusted** distributed computing
  - Workers CAN communicate freely
  - Shared memory for performance
  - Ideal for ML training across GPUs

  **Modal**: Designed for **untrusted** code execution
  - Containers are ISOLATED by design
  - Security > Performance
  - Ideal for running user/LLM code safely
end note

@enduml
